  interpreter/*.in.dbml   <- packages/dbml-parse/__tests__/snapshots/interpreter/input/
  interpreter/*.out.json  <- packages/dbml-parse/__tests__/snapshots/interpreter/output/
  {lexer,parser,validator,binder,nan}/*.in.dbml, *.out.json, infinite_loops/*.in.dbml
                          <- packages/dbml-parse/__tests__/snapshots/{lexer,parser,validator,binder}/{input,output}/
  dbml-core/exporter/{mysql,postgres,mssql}_exporter/{input,output}/
                          <- packages/dbml-core/__tests__/examples/exporter/
  dbml-core/importer/{mysql,postgres,mssql}_importer/{input,output}/
                          <- packages/dbml-core/__tests__/examples/importer/
  dbml-core/parser/{mysql,postgres,mssql,schemarb}-parse/{input,output}/
                          <- packages/dbml-core/__tests__/examples/parser/

They are used unmodified as golden conformance suites by conformance_test.go,
diagnostics_conformance_test.go and (as inputs whose @dbml/core 10.3.1 output
is regenerated by scripts/reference/{export,import}.mjs) export/ and importer/.

Portions of go-dbml (lexer, parser, and the semantic rules in model/) are
derived from the Apache-2.0 licensed @dbml/parse source in the same repository.
